WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:07.657
♪♪

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:08.558
&gt;&gt;&gt; Florida governor Ron

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:10.393
Desantis is now providing the

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:11.895
clearest indication yet of where

00:00:12.028 --> 00:00:13.863
he stands on a major foreign

00:00:13.997 --> 00:00:15.331
policy issue.

00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:16.733
Desantis telling Fox News's

00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:18.902
tucker Carlson he disagrees

00:00:19.335 --> 00:00:20.603
where most in his party are in

00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:22.472
Ukraine, putting it this way.

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:23.873
Saying, quote, while the U.S.

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:26.242
Has many vital national

00:00:26.376 --> 00:00:27.644
interests, skurg our borders,

00:00:27.777 --> 00:00:28.745
addressing the crisis of

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:30.380
readiness with our military,

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:31.347
achieving energy security and

00:00:31.347 --> 00:00:35.919
Independence and checking the

00:00:36.052 --> 00:00:36.986
economic cultural military power

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:40.490
of the Chinese communist party,

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:47.363
becoming involved in a

00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:47.931
territorial dispute with Russia

00:00:48.064 --> 00:00:49.599
and Ukraine is not one of them.

00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:50.900
Desantis has not announced he's

00:00:51.034 --> 00:00:51.401
running with.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:52.936
Put that in context with what

00:00:53.369 --> 00:00:55.972
Desantis said back in 2015.

00:00:56.105 --> 00:00:57.373
This was after Russia illegally

00:00:57.373 --> 00:00:58.074
annexed crimea.

00:00:58.208 --> 00:00:59.375
He was then a congressman and

00:00:59.442 --> 00:01:00.476
this is what he said at the

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:00.777
time.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:01.678
We in the congress have been

00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:03.379
urging the president, referring

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.914
to president Obama, to provide

00:01:05.048 --> 00:01:05.748
arms to Ukraine.

00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:07.050
They want to fight their good

00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:07.483
fight.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.618
They're not asking us to fight

00:01:08.751 --> 00:01:09.452
it for them.

00:01:09.586 --> 00:01:10.820
And the president has

00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:11.654
steadfastly refused.

00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:14.357
I think that's a mistake.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.927
&gt;&gt; And governor Ron Desantis,

00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:18.628
former president trump's most

00:01:18.761 --> 00:01:19.395
frequent target on the campaign

00:01:19.495 --> 00:01:21.764
trail in Iowa.

00:01:21.898 --> 00:01:23.433
So CNN's Kristen Holmes live now

00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:24.901
in Davenport with more on this.

00:01:25.034 --> 00:01:26.135
Kristen, good morning to you.

00:01:26.269 --> 00:01:27.971
How did trump's first Iowa stop

00:01:28.104 --> 00:01:31.407
go, full of jokes, I'm sure.

00:01:31.507 --> 00:01:32.408
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Good morning, don.

00:01:32.542 --> 00:01:33.409
Well, this was really the first

00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:36.813
time we heard him go after

00:01:36.946 --> 00:01:38.014
Desantis by name in a speech

00:01:38.147 --> 00:01:39.916
since he announced his candidacy

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:41.417
for president.

00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.619
Usually he saves that for his

00:01:42.752 --> 00:01:44.087
social media page or for these

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.521
one on one interviews.

00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:46.990
And I will say that while it was

00:01:47.423 --> 00:01:49.892
a very enthusiastic night, the

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:51.628
response to those criticisms of

00:01:51.761 --> 00:01:53.029
the Florida governor was a

00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:54.063
little bit lukewarm.

00:01:54.197 --> 00:01:55.965
It was clear from people that we

00:01:56.099 --> 00:01:56.966
talked to that while they like

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.835
trump and maybe they like trump

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.470
better, they still like Florida

00:02:00.603 --> 00:02:01.437
governor Ron Desantis.

00:02:01.437 --> 00:02:02.739
But one thing was very clear in

00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:05.008
the last two days we spent here.

00:02:05.441 --> 00:02:05.908
We talked to people.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:07.043
We saw the crowd last night.

00:02:07.443 --> 00:02:09.012
It was a packed house for Donald

00:02:09.445 --> 00:02:09.512
Trump.

00:02:09.512 --> 00:02:12.248
And, of course, those CNN poll

00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:13.883
numbers, Donald Trump is still a

00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:17.620
huge force in the Republican

00:02:17.754 --> 00:02:18.388
party.

00:02:18.521 --> 00:02:19.088
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Former president

00:02:19.455 --> 00:02:22.492
Donald Trump taking aim at

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:25.628
Florida governor Ron Desantis in

00:02:25.762 --> 00:02:25.928
Iowa.

00:02:26.062 --> 00:02:28.197
&gt;&gt; Ron desantus.

00:02:28.331 --> 00:02:28.898
&gt;&gt; Reporter: During his first

00:02:29.032 --> 00:02:30.633
trip to the crucial early state

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:32.302
since announcing his third white

00:02:32.435 --> 00:02:32.702
house bid.

00:02:32.835 --> 00:02:37.940
&gt;&gt; Ron was a disciple of Paul

00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:38.241
Ryan.

00:02:38.374 --> 00:02:40.109
Who is a rhino loser who

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.211
currently is destroying fox and

00:02:42.345 --> 00:02:45.848
would constantly vote against

00:02:45.982 --> 00:02:46.282
entitlements.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:46.949
&gt;&gt; Reporter: At this early

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:47.684
stage, Desantis is widely seen

00:02:47.817 --> 00:02:49.152
as the former president's chief

00:02:49.485 --> 00:02:51.688
rival for the GOP nomination.

00:02:51.821 --> 00:02:53.856
&gt;&gt; Ron Desantis strongly opposed

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:54.190
ethanal.

00:02:54.324 --> 00:02:55.958
Do you know that?

00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:57.727
And we don't even know if he's

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.061
running.

00:02:58.194 --> 00:02:59.762
But I might as well tell you, if

00:02:59.896 --> 00:03:03.132
he's not rung, I will say he was

00:03:03.499 --> 00:03:03.733
fine on ethanal.

00:03:03.866 --> 00:03:04.567
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The Florida

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.235
governor has yet to announce a

00:03:06.369 --> 00:03:07.036
presidential run.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.137
Earlier in the evening, trump

00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:09.906
setting his sights on another

00:03:10.039 --> 00:03:10.907
potential 2024 hopeful.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.509
His former running mate, while

00:03:13.576 --> 00:03:15.044
seeking to deflect blame for the

00:03:15.178 --> 00:03:17.847
violent attack on the capitol on

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:18.247
January 6th.

00:03:18.381 --> 00:03:19.716
Telling "The Washington post"

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:21.517
that Mike pence was at least in

00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:22.018
part to blame for the events

00:03:22.151 --> 00:03:23.519
that day.

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:25.054
Saying, quote, had he sent the

00:03:25.188 --> 00:03:26.622
votes back to the legislatures,

00:03:26.756 --> 00:03:27.857
they wouldn't have had a problem

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.525
with January 6th.

00:03:29.525 --> 00:03:31.728
So in many ways, you can blame

00:03:31.861 --> 00:03:33.796
him for January 6th.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.531
Trump's comments in response to

00:03:35.531 --> 00:03:36.799
the former vice president

00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:38.134
delivering his sharpest rebuke

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.703
yet of his former boss in a

00:03:40.837 --> 00:03:42.338
private speech during an annual

00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:43.806
dinner in Washington, pence

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.641
telling attendees, quote, I know

00:03:45.775 --> 00:03:47.710
that history will hold Donald

00:03:47.844 --> 00:03:49.779
Trump accountable for January

00:03:49.912 --> 00:03:50.380
6th.

00:03:50.513 --> 00:03:52.782
Trump becoming the latest 2024

00:03:52.915 --> 00:03:54.784
Republican hopeful to visit

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:55.084
Iowa.

00:03:55.218 --> 00:03:56.853
&gt;&gt; The agricultural industry

00:03:56.986 --> 00:03:58.855
should be treated just like the

00:03:58.988 --> 00:03:59.555
manufacturing industry.

00:03:59.589 --> 00:04:00.923
&gt;&gt; We said we are going to go on

00:04:01.057 --> 00:04:01.557
offense.

00:04:01.557 --> 00:04:02.425
I'm going to find issues.

00:04:02.558 --> 00:04:04.460
&gt;&gt; Reporter: As the 2024 GOP

00:04:04.594 --> 00:04:06.829
field begins to take shape.

00:04:06.963 --> 00:04:08.598
A new CNN poll showing that the

00:04:08.731 --> 00:04:10.032
former president still remains a

00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:12.668
leading figure in the party.

00:04:12.802 --> 00:04:14.637
40% of Republicans and

00:04:14.771 --> 00:04:15.571
republican-leaning independents

00:04:15.638 --> 00:04:17.940
said they would most likely back

00:04:18.074 --> 00:04:19.842
trump for the GOP nomination

00:04:19.976 --> 00:04:21.577
when given a list of nine

00:04:21.577 --> 00:04:23.079
potential candidates.

00:04:23.212 --> 00:04:25.715
Compared to the 36% who chose

00:04:25.848 --> 00:04:26.949
Florida governor Ron Desantis.

00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:29.585
The only two to reach double

00:04:29.585 --> 00:04:29.619
digits.

00:04:29.752 --> 00:04:31.921
With former vice president pence

00:04:32.054 --> 00:04:33.723
and former U.N. Ambassador Nikki

00:04:33.856 --> 00:04:37.760
Haley at 6% each.

00:04:37.894 --> 00:04:39.028
&gt;&gt; And don, of course it is

00:04:39.162 --> 00:04:40.396
important to note that this is

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.798
still very early.

00:04:41.931 --> 00:04:42.832
Obviously the former vice

00:04:42.965 --> 00:04:44.033
president as well as the Florida

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.201
governor have not even announced

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:46.669
that they are going to be

00:04:46.803 --> 00:04:47.603
running for president.

00:04:47.603 --> 00:04:49.772
Even though, of course, that is

00:04:49.906 --> 00:04:50.173
anticipated.

00:04:50.306 --> 00:04:52.041
But this is expected to be a

00:04:52.175 --> 00:04:53.609
very crowded GOP field.

00:04:53.609 --> 00:04:55.611
And it's expected to be a very

00:04:55.611 --> 00:04:56.813
busy next year and a half.

00:04:56.946 --> 00:04:57.079
Don?

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:59.982
&gt;&gt; Right on that, Kristen.

00:05:00.116 --> 00:05:01.617
Yet here we are covering them.

00:05:01.717 --> 00:05:02.318
Thank you so much.

00:05:02.552 --> 00:05:06.055
I wonder if we should make --

00:05:06.189 --> 00:05:07.723
unless they declare, should we

00:05:07.857 --> 00:05:09.625
not talk about them as if they

00:05:09.759 --> 00:05:10.259
are running?

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:11.828
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:11.961 --> 00:05:13.629
Until you declare --

00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:15.932
&gt;&gt; 36% of people in that poll

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:16.265
want --

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:17.633
&gt;&gt; We could have done that last

00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:18.768
year or the year before.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.136
&gt;&gt; Kind of reminds me of what

00:05:20.269 --> 00:05:20.970
trump said last night.

00:05:21.103 --> 00:05:22.205
He was saying that Desantis is

00:05:22.338 --> 00:05:24.340
bad on ethanal.

00:05:24.474 --> 00:05:26.542
He said, but unless he doesn't

00:05:26.676 --> 00:05:29.645
run for president I'll say he's

00:05:29.645 --> 00:05:30.446
good on ethanal.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.783
&gt;&gt; We got a fourth guest to the

00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:34.083
table.

00:05:34.217 --> 00:05:34.484
&gt;&gt; Hi.

00:05:34.617 --> 00:05:36.552
He is CNN political analyst and

00:05:36.686 --> 00:05:38.120
national politics reporter for

00:05:38.254 --> 00:05:38.855
"The New York Times" as well.

00:05:38.988 --> 00:05:39.655
Good morning to you.

00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:39.956
&gt;&gt; Good morning.

00:05:40.089 --> 00:05:41.324
I also loved that trump line on

00:05:41.657 --> 00:05:41.891
Desantis.

00:05:42.024 --> 00:05:43.326
Just showing how transactional

00:05:43.659 --> 00:05:45.294
his politics really is.

00:05:45.661 --> 00:05:46.996
&gt;&gt; So I said what are you hot

00:05:47.129 --> 00:05:47.263
on?

00:05:47.663 --> 00:05:49.665
&gt;&gt; I think that this

00:05:49.699 --> 00:05:50.233
presidential race is really

00:05:50.366 --> 00:05:51.300
turning up to another level.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:52.602
Over the weekend we had that

00:05:52.735 --> 00:05:53.936
back and forth between former

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:55.671
president trump and Mike pence,

00:05:55.671 --> 00:05:57.874
which is not new, those lines of

00:05:58.007 --> 00:05:58.207
attack.

00:05:58.341 --> 00:05:59.909
President trump has been blaming

00:06:00.042 --> 00:06:01.143
Mike pence wrongly for the

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:04.013
attacks on January 6th for

00:06:04.146 --> 00:06:04.313
years.

00:06:04.447 --> 00:06:05.681
He was doing that on that day.

00:06:05.781 --> 00:06:07.083
Publicly doing it privately.

00:06:07.216 --> 00:06:08.317
But we have now seen vice

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:09.719
president pence ramp up his kind

00:06:09.852 --> 00:06:11.687
of positioning as he gets closer

00:06:11.687 --> 00:06:12.622
to the presidential race.

00:06:12.755 --> 00:06:14.690
He took out a kind of

00:06:14.824 --> 00:06:16.225
pro-ukraine position, which

00:06:16.359 --> 00:06:17.793
obviously cuts against some of

00:06:17.927 --> 00:06:19.095
the Republican electorate.

00:06:19.228 --> 00:06:21.697
And now with that gridiron,

00:06:21.697 --> 00:06:23.099
replacing Washington, D.C. Where

00:06:23.232 --> 00:06:23.833
there was going to be a lot of

00:06:23.966 --> 00:06:25.101
media folks there, he ramped up

00:06:25.234 --> 00:06:27.069
those attacks Donald Trump and

00:06:27.203 --> 00:06:27.703
democracy.

00:06:27.703 --> 00:06:29.105
I think this is someone on vice

00:06:29.238 --> 00:06:30.106
president pence side who may

00:06:30.239 --> 00:06:32.575
have been trying to pick that

00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:33.709
fight with Donald Trump, draw

00:06:33.709 --> 00:06:34.610
him into the race growing his

00:06:34.744 --> 00:06:36.412
own lane, growing his own

00:06:36.546 --> 00:06:38.080
position as he heads into 2024.

00:06:38.214 --> 00:06:41.017
The race is definitely turning

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:41.284
up.

00:06:41.717 --> 00:06:41.984
&gt;&gt; It certainly is.

00:06:42.118 --> 00:06:44.353
Part of that with the pence

00:06:44.487 --> 00:06:46.289
calculus of why he did that is

00:06:46.422 --> 00:06:47.990
now other Republicans are going

00:06:48.124 --> 00:06:49.725
to get asked about their view of

00:06:49.725 --> 00:06:50.960
January 6th and if trump will be

00:06:51.093 --> 00:06:52.194
held accountable that day.

00:06:52.328 --> 00:06:53.262
Trump's response, I want to go

00:06:53.396 --> 00:06:54.397
back to that for a moment

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.298
because I don't think we

00:06:55.731 --> 00:06:56.299
focussed on it enough here this

00:06:56.432 --> 00:06:57.800
morning which is he is blaming

00:06:57.934 --> 00:06:59.068
Mike pence, saying that the

00:06:59.201 --> 00:07:01.170
actions he did not take that day

00:07:01.304 --> 00:07:05.207
is why they was January 6th.

00:07:05.341 --> 00:07:07.209
That's what he told reporters on

00:07:07.343 --> 00:07:09.745
the plane to Iowa.

00:07:09.745 --> 00:07:13.783
That's the same argument John

00:07:13.916 --> 00:07:15.251
Eastman made to pence's counsel

00:07:15.384 --> 00:07:16.619
saying this is your boss's fault

00:07:16.752 --> 00:07:17.853
because he didn't do what we

00:07:17.987 --> 00:07:18.688
wanted him to do.

00:07:18.821 --> 00:07:19.889
That's why we're seeing this

00:07:20.022 --> 00:07:20.456
level of violence.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.390
&gt;&gt; Exactly.

00:07:21.757 --> 00:07:23.092
From that day all until now,

00:07:23.225 --> 00:07:25.061
despite all of the evidence

00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:26.462
that's come out, despite the

00:07:26.596 --> 00:07:27.763
facts, Donald Trump and those

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:29.932
around him, the hardened trump

00:07:30.066 --> 00:07:31.300
base, has not changed their

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:32.501
position here.

00:07:32.635 --> 00:07:34.437
They still blame Mike pence for

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:35.771
those actions and not sending

00:07:35.871 --> 00:07:37.873
the certification back to the

00:07:38.007 --> 00:07:39.342
state legislatures, something

00:07:39.775 --> 00:07:40.576
pence did not have the authority

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:41.777
to pull off on that day.

00:07:41.911 --> 00:07:44.180
And so, when I was just at CPAC,

00:07:44.313 --> 00:07:46.482
again a representation of the

00:07:46.616 --> 00:07:48.417
hardened, collective trump base,

00:07:48.551 --> 00:07:50.152
this is still the line of attack

00:07:50.286 --> 00:07:50.686
on pence.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.789
They are defending the rioters

00:07:53.789 --> 00:07:54.557
January 6th.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:55.858
Actually saw folks in shirts

00:07:55.992 --> 00:07:56.959
that were really supporting

00:07:57.093 --> 00:07:59.161
those people, making sure they

00:07:59.295 --> 00:08:00.396
went up to people who talked on

00:08:00.529 --> 00:08:01.931
the stage, making sure they

00:08:02.064 --> 00:08:02.865
pulled Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:08:02.999 --> 00:08:03.799
over to the side.

00:08:03.799 --> 00:08:06.002
Making sure that that issue

00:08:06.135 --> 00:08:07.003
stayed in the consciousness of

00:08:07.136 --> 00:08:08.037
some of those people.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.372
And I think there was an

00:08:09.805 --> 00:08:11.073
interesting split screen at CPAC

00:08:11.207 --> 00:08:12.141
actually which speaks to this

00:08:12.274 --> 00:08:13.809
point from the stage, you did

00:08:13.809 --> 00:08:15.811
not really hear election denial

00:08:15.811 --> 00:08:17.246
January 6th come up that much.

